  the same amplitude fit on KT2017's Nm=2 pairs (20-500 kpc, N = 303): A = 1.06 (+0.023 dex) against 1.74 (+0.242 dex) for the independent 2MRS sample
  [PASS] 48b ⚠ A FALSE WIN AVOIDED.  Run naively on the catalogue the hunt list names, item 48 would have reported the deep-MOND two-body law fitting with amplitude A ~ 1 and no free parameter -- a clean hit.  It is manufactured: Kourkchi & Tully link galaxies inside a velocity window scaled by the K-band luminosity, so the catalogue contains only pairs whose dv was small enough to be linked, and the same estimator on an independently selected sample of the same galaxies at the same separations and masses gives a much larger dispersion.  Item 48 as posed cannot be run on that catalogue   (KT2017 A = 1.06 (would read as a hit); independent 2MRS A = 1.74; ratio 0.60)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SYSTEMATICS THAT ARE NOT IN THE ERROR BARS, stated plainly:
   1. ISOLATION DEPTH is the big one (see the completeness caveat above).  Widening R_iso from 800 to 2500 kpc
      does nothing, but going DEEPER does: the amplitude excess falls from 1.99 in the far shell to 1.51 in the
      near one, where 2MRS reaches four times further down the luminosity function.  2MRS cannot exclude fainter
      companions or an intra-group medium, and those are baryons the framework is allowed to use, so 69c's
      offset is an UPPER LIMIT on the framework's real deficit here.  It does not reach zero within this data.
   2. distances are cz_CMB/H0; a 300 km/s peculiar velocity is 10% in D at cz = 3000, so r_p and L_K carry a
      distance systematic which is worst at small separation, where the flatness test has its lever.
   3. Upsilon_K = 0.6 is assumed.  The amplitude moves as Upsilon_K^(1/4) in the framework, so the 69c offset
      would need Upsilon_K ~ 3-4 to close -- far outside any stellar population.
   4. gas is not counted in M_b.  20% of M* raises the framework prediction by 0.02 dex in velocity.
   5. circular relative orbits are assumed.  Eccentric orbits with the same energy spend more time near
      apocentre at LOWER speed, so this assumption is generous to the framework, not stingy.
   6. the external field is a single nominal e_N = 0.03 for every pair; a per-pair value from 2M++ would only
      move the framework's prediction DOWN, away from the data.

